# Export period type vs P&L banner

## Invariant

**Period Type** (and Period label) on exported Excel must describe the **same start/end** as the Biz Intel P&L banner — not a binary Monthly/Quarterly flag derived from range length.

| Banner selection | Period Type | Period label example |
|------------------|-------------|----------------------|
| Exact month | Monthly | March 2026 |
| Exact BAS Q1–Q4 | Quarterly | Q4 2025-2026 |
| Exact AU FY (1 Jul–30 Jun) | Financial Year | FY 2025-2026 |
| Full statement / custom | Custom | 07/12/2025 – 29/06/2026 |

## Bug class

`daysDiff <= 35 ? monthly : quarterly` labeled **every** long window as Quarterly — including Financial Year. GST amounts could still be correct while the header lied.

## Do

- Classify with `resolveBasReportPeriodMeta` / exact month·quarter·FY matchers
- Print via `formatBasPeriodTypeLabel`
- Test FY + one custom range + Q1–Q4

## Do not

- Infer Period Type from day count alone
- Snap FY to Q1 of 1 July (separate bug — see `accounting-export-bas-gst.mdc`)
